WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:17.289
Tommy noticed that the storm had stopped long ago.

2
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.234
He told the doctor that he should go home.

3
00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:24.051
"You have to eat something," insisted Dr. Dolittle.

4
00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:27.026
"It's a long walk back to your house."

5
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.822
So Tommy stayed for dinner.

6
00:00:29.823 --> 00:00:34.465
During the meal, Polynesia explained why she had returned.

7
00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:38.593
"I miss the adventure and excitement!" she said.

8
00:00:38.594 --> 00:00:45.744
"I will always love Africa, but I miss going on voyages with you, Doctor."

9
00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:50.783
"Will you be going on another voyage soon, Dr. Dolittle?" asked Tommy.

10
00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.870
The doctor pushed away his empty plate.

11
00:00:53.871 --> 00:00:58.651
"Well, I must say, I've been thinking about . . ." he began.

12
00:00:58.652 --> 00:01:05.137
But before he had a chance to answer, an owl flew into the room.

13
00:01:05.138 --> 00:01:09.533
"Oh, hello, Too-Too," the doctor said in greeting.

14
00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.175
"You're up early!"

15
00:01:11.176 --> 00:01:14.910
"Welcome home, Dr. Dolittle!" the owl hooted.

16
00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:17.805
Dr. Dolittle ran to the window.

17
00:01:17.806 --> 00:01:20.997
"Oh, dear! Tommy, we'd better get going.

18
00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:23.619
It's already dark outside."

19
00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.169
"I'll come with you," said Polynesia.

20
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.698
It was very late when they finally arrived at Tommy's house.

21
00:01:32.699 --> 00:01:35.881
His mother was quite worried and upset.

22
00:01:35.882 --> 00:01:40.413
"It's my fault, Mrs. Stubbins," apologized Dr. Dolittle.

23
00:01:40.414 --> 00:01:44.976
Tommy's mother stared at the little man with the parrot on his shoulder.

24
00:01:44.977 --> 00:01:50.159
"And who might you be, sir?" she asked.

25
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.842
Dr. Dolittle introduced himself.

26
00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:56.693
Then he stuck out his foot and pointed to his boots.

27
00:01:56.694 --> 00:02:01.373
"These were made by your husband, a very fine shoemaker indeed."

28
00:02:01.374 --> 00:02:03.526
Tommy's father blushed.

29
00:02:03.527 --> 00:02:08.598
"Thank you, sir. Won't you come in for some tea?" he invited.

30
00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:12.857
"Dr. Dolittle's come to look at the squirrel," said Tommy.

31
00:02:12.858 --> 00:02:17.567
"Tommy is always bringing home little animals," his mother said.

32
00:02:17.568 --> 00:02:22.275
"Perhaps he will grow up to be an animal doctor," the doctor exclaimed.

33
00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:26.078
"Doctor? Oh, no, sir," his father replied.

34
00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:29.178
"We don't have money to send Tommy to school."

35
00:02:29.179 --> 00:02:33.094
On hearing this, Tommy felt disappointed.

36
00:02:33.095 --> 00:02:36.740
Tommy took the doctor and Polynesia to his room.

37
00:02:36.741 --> 00:02:39.704
He tried not to show how upset he was.

38
00:02:39.705 --> 00:02:43.520
It was true—Tommy's family was very poor.

39
00:02:43.521 --> 00:02:48.051
They couldn't afford to send Tommy to school.

40
00:02:48.052 --> 00:02:49.487
"Here is the squirrel."

41
00:02:49.488 --> 00:02:51.733
Tommy held out the box.

42
00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:57.498
Dr. Dolittle peered inside and started making strange squeaky noises.

43
00:02:57.499 --> 00:03:01.453
"Hello, little friend," he was saying to the squirrel.

44
00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:06.718
"Oh, it's the great Dr. Dolittle," the squirrel said weakly.

45
00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.269
"Where does it hurt?"

46
00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.455
The doctor poked its leg gently.

47
00:03:12.456 --> 00:03:15.953
Tommy had wrapped the squirrel's leg in a bandage.

48
00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:19.806
"I thought his leg might be hurt," Tommy explained.

49
00:03:19.807 --> 00:03:21.292
The doctor nodded.

50
00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:22.904
"Yes, you did well.

51
00:03:22.905 --> 00:03:25.407
His leg is indeed hurt."

52
00:03:25.408 --> 00:03:31.982
"Tommy! Listen carefully to the squirrel," Polynesia instructed.

53
00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:36.724
Tommy bent down lower, but all he heard were squeaks.

54
00:03:36.725 --> 00:03:40.170
"I can't understand," he sighed.

55
00:03:40.171 --> 00:03:45.167
"Animal talk is more than just sounds," explained Polynesia.

56
00:03:45.168 --> 00:03:52.007
"Look at its gestures, its movements, and try to think like the squirrel."

57
00:03:52.008 --> 00:03:57.118
For the next few minutes, Tommy kept his eyes focused on the squirrel.

58
00:03:57.119 --> 00:03:59.964
Finally he jumped up and said:

59
00:03:59.965 --> 00:04:02.273
"He was attacked by a bird.

60
00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.321
He was hurt by a bird!"

61
00:04:04.322 --> 00:04:09.663
"Excellent, Tommy! And what else?" Polynesia said encouragingly.

62
00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:14.021
Tommy turned his attention back to the squirrel.

63
00:04:14.022 --> 00:04:16.965
"Well, uh," Tommy stammered.

64
00:04:16.966 --> 00:04:21.439
"The bird chased him up a tree, and then he found a delicious looking nut . . ."

65
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.545
Dr. Dolittle and Polynesia looked at each other and tried not to laugh.

66
00:04:27.546 --> 00:04:31.424
"Not quite, Tommy," coughed Dr. Dolittle.

67
00:04:31.425 --> 00:04:33.780
"The bird took the squirrel's nut.

68
00:04:33.781 --> 00:04:36.688
But you were right about the bird attacking."

69
00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:46.060
"Doctor, I believe that Tommy may have the gift after all," Polynesia remarked. Tommy smiled.

70
00:04:46.061 --> 00:04:52.045
A little while later, Dr. Dolittle and Polynesia waved good-bye to their new friends.

71
00:04:52.046 --> 00:04:59.067
"I think one day Tommy could become an animal doctor like you," whispered Polynesia.

72
00:04:59.068 --> 00:05:01.739
"Yes," the doctor agreed.

73
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:08.160
"I wonder what we can do to help him."
